    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "General information on the variances and covariances of moments can be found in Chapter 10 of Kendall and Stuart (1977). Letting $ m_r = n^{-1} \\sum (x_i - \\overline{x})^r $ and $ \\mu_r = E[(x - \\mu_x)^r] $ represent observations and expectations for the $ r $th moment about the mean, the following approximations apply to the sampling variances and covariances,",
      "source_page": 827,
      "printed_page": 807,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p009:b9"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        47.0,
        724.0,
        1006.0,
        885.0
      ],
