    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ \\mu_{0} = \\mu_{1} = 0 $. Ideally, in the application of any of these formulae, unbiased estimates of the moments $ (\\mu_{r}) $ should be employed (as illustrated in Examples 3 and 5). A few other useful results from Kendall and Stuart (1977) follow.",
      "source_page": 827,
      "printed_page": 807,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p009:b13"
      ],
      "bbox": [
