    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where Skw(x), given as Equation 2.7 in the text, is an unbiased estimate of the third moment. For symmetrical distributions, such as the normal, all odd moments have expectations equal to zero, in which case the covariance between mean and variance is zero.",
